-- title:
--   Torsion-freeness of A/pA over R/(p) for integral extensions
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $A$ be commutative Noetherian integrally closed domains (in the same universe), with $A$ an $R$-algebra whose structure map $R \to A$ is injective (the `FaithfulSMul` hypothesis) and which is integral over $R$. Let $p \in R$ be such that the principal ideal $(p) = \operatorname{span}\{p\}$ is prime and $p \neq 0$, and let $s \in R$ with $s \notin (p)$. Then for every $a \in A$ such that the image of $s$ in $A$ times $a$ lies in the ideal of $A$ generated by the image of $p$, already $a$ lies in that ideal. Equivalently: if $s a \in pA$ with $s \in R \setminus pR$, then $a \in pA$; that is, $A/pA$ is torsion-free as a module over the domain $R/(p)$, the torsion being taken with respect to the non-zero elements of $R/(p)$ coming from $R$.
--
--   The statement expresses that, for an integral extension of Noetherian normal domains and a prime principal ideal $(p)$ of the base, no element of $R \setminus (p)$ becomes a zero-divisor on $A/pA$; it is the standard torsion-freeness (or absence of embedded and badly placed associated primes) input for reduction modulo $p$ of integral extensions. It is used in the proofs of [`IsIntegrallyClosed.isReduced_quotient_span_singleton_of_squarefree_minpoly`](thm.html#IsIntegrallyClosed.isReduced_quotient_span_singleton_of_squarefree_minpoly), [`IsIntegrallyClosed.ringKrullDim_localization_tensor_eq_one_of_irreducible`](thm.html#IsIntegrallyClosed.ringKrullDim_localization_tensor_eq_one_of_irreducible) and [`Subalgebra.isReduced_tensor_of_separable`](thm.html#Subalgebra.isReduced_tensor_of_separable).
